From cadd9482aae260ade47be0eb4d2ac020b03c8583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ArtCraft's mark on the Start button and the PS5 tile

The Mihawk mark (a white squircle, an amber frame, a navy M) was the Start
button and the title's icon. ArtCraft's is a painter's colour wheel,
original to this edition: one ring sector per Craft app in its colour,
ordered by hue, the first at the top, three degrees apart, around a white hub
with a grey rim. One geometry, drawn four ways as the fork already drew its
mark, so the tests keep tying them together:
  - themes/windows11/start.svg, the reference (13 paths and a circle);
  - ps5/tools/icon0.svg, the mark on a dark tile, and ps5/sce_sys/icon0.png,
    that SVG rendered by librsvg at 512 x 512 as 8-bit RGB;
  - src/pw_taskbar_logo.h, the Start button at any size without libm: a
    sample is in a sector when it is in the ring and on the inner side of
    both of the sector's edges (two cross products against unit vectors
    written as constants), each shape antialiased by 16 x 16 samples and
    composed as an SVG renderer composes them.
All four are written by PS5-ARTCRAFT's artcraft_ps5/mark.py from
edition/suite.json's colours.

tests/test_title_icon.py reads the new shapes (paths, a circle) and the dark
tile; tests/test_taskbar_logo.py checks the shape is left-right symmetric
(its colours are not), the corner clear, the hub white and the top sector
its colour.

Proven: tests/test_taskbar_logo.py and tests/test_title_icon.py pass with
librsvg 2.58 installed, so against the SVG: mean error 1.44 levels at 22 px
(96 DPI), 0.62 at 33, 0.66 at 44; 95 to 97 % of pixels within 8 (the test's
limits: 1.5 and 90 %; the Mihawk mark measured 1.36 at 22). No console run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ErqzkhbC5fRkeGcCmR5R95
