- * squircle (1 to 99, rx 30) under a 2-unit #C9D3DD stroke, a 2-unit amber frame (6 to 94, rx 25) and a navy M, an
- * 11-unit stroke through 25,80.5 25,34.5 50,64.5 75,34.5 75,80.5 with mitred corners and butt ends. The taskbar draws it
- * at every DPI, 22 px at 96 (Wine patch 1162). Each shape is antialiased by 16 x 16 samples.
+ * The Start button's ArtCraft mark at any size, as themes/windows11/start.svg draws it in its 100-unit box: 13 ring
+ * sectors (radius 27 to 47 around 50,50, 3 degrees apart), one per Craft app in its colour, and a white hub (radius 13)
+ * under a 2-unit #C9D3DD rim. Written by PS5-ARTCRAFT's artcraft_ps5/mark.py with the SVG, so the two agree. The
+ * taskbar draws it at every DPI, 22 px at 96 (Wine patch 1162). Each shape is antialiased by 16 x 16 samples; a sector
+ * is the ring between its two edges, told by the signs of two cross products (no trigonometry: Explorer has no libm).
  *
  * Output: extent x extent premultiplied BGRA words (0xAARRGGBB), as GdiAlphaBlend takes them. tests/test_taskbar_logo.py
  * compares it with librsvg's drawing of start.svg. */
